      <div id="list-item-5" class="faq-block">
      
      <h2>FAQ</h2>

                                                                            
      <div class="views-element-container">
  <div  class="faqs faqs-product view view-faqs view-id-faqs view-display-id-faq_product js-view-dom-id-a38a1cb6b8b753b348a74e2fd6621536b93bd08de1b11f347618185b13aeef01">
  
    
      
      <div itemscope itemtype="https://schema.org/FAQPage" class="view-content">
      <div>
  
  <ul class="container-collapse">

          <li>

    
    <div class="views-field views-field-title"><span class="field-content">  <div itemscope itemprop="mainEntity" itemtype="https://schema.org/Question">
    <h3 itemprop="name" class='collapse-title collapsed' data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse-faq-63929" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapseExample">
      What is the Ecosoft AQUABOX 150 and what is its purpose?
    </h3>
    <div itemscope itemprop="acceptedAnswer" itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer" class="collapse" id="collapse-faq-63929">
      <div class="card card-body mt-3">
        <div itemprop="text">
          <p>The <strong>Ecosoft AQUABOX 150 </strong>is a water vending machine designed to purify mains water to bottled-water quality, compliant with Directive 2020/2184/EU, and automatically dispense it into consumers' bottles.</p><p>It includes <strong>multiple purification stages</strong>: mechanical filtration, activated carbon filtration, reverse osmosis membrane separation, remineralisation, additional carbon filtration for taste improvement, and UV disinfection.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</span></div></li>
          <li>

    
    <div class="views-field views-field-title"><span class="field-content">  <div itemscope itemprop="mainEntity" itemtype="https://schema.org/Question">
    <h3 itemprop="name" class='collapse-title collapsed' data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse-faq-63930" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapseExample">
      How does the machine purify the water?
    </h3>
    <div itemscope itemprop="acceptedAnswer" itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer" class="collapse" id="collapse-faq-63930">
      <div class="card card-body mt-3">
        <div itemprop="text">
          <p>Water purification involves <strong>several stages</strong>: <strong>mechanical filtration</strong> to remove suspended particles, <strong>activated carbon</strong> to eliminate chlorine, <strong>antiscalant </strong>to prevent scaling on membranes, high-pressure <strong>reverse osmosis</strong> to reduce salts, microorganisms, and bacteria, <strong>remineralisation </strong>to adjust mineral content, <strong>post-carbon filtration</strong> for improved taste and odour, and <strong>UV disinfection</strong>.</p><p>Purified water is stored in a pressure tank before dispensing.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</span></div></li>
          <li>

    
    <div class="views-field views-field-title"><span class="field-content">  <div itemscope itemprop="mainEntity" itemtype="https://schema.org/Question">
    <h3 itemprop="name" class='collapse-title collapsed' data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse-faq-63931" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapseExample">
      What payment methods does the machine accept?
    </h3>
    <div itemscope itemprop="acceptedAnswer" itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer" class="collapse" id="collapse-faq-63931">
      <div class="card card-body mt-3">
        <div itemprop="text">
          <p>The standard configuration includes a <strong>QR code reader</strong> for contactless payments.</p><p>Optional features include a bill acceptor, coin acceptor, and POS terminal allowing payments by cash, coins, or card, depending on the installed options.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</span></div></li>
          <li>

    
    <div class="views-field views-field-title"><span class="field-content">  <div itemscope itemprop="mainEntity" itemtype="https://schema.org/Question">
    <h3 itemprop="name" class='collapse-title collapsed' data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse-faq-63932" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapseExample">
      Is the water dispensed by the machine safe to drink?
    </h3>
    <div itemscope itemprop="acceptedAnswer" itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer" class="collapse" id="collapse-faq-63932">
      <div class="card card-body mt-3">
        <div itemprop="text">
          <p>Yes. The purified water <strong>meets bottled water standards</strong> under Directive 2020/2184/EU and Ukraine’s sanitary-epidemiological requirements (Report No. 602-123-20-1/3637).</p><p>It undergoes rigorous treatment — including filtration, membrane separation, remineralisation, and UV disinfection — to remove impurities, chlorine, salts, bacteria, and microorganisms.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</span></div></li>
          <li>

    
    <div class="views-field views-field-title"><span class="field-content">  <div itemscope itemprop="mainEntity" itemtype="https://schema.org/Question">
    <h3 itemprop="name" class='collapse-title collapsed' data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse-faq-63934" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapseExample">
      What are the requirements for installing the machine?
    </h3>
    <div itemscope itemprop="acceptedAnswer" itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer" class="collapse" id="collapse-faq-63934">
      <div class="card card-body mt-3">
        <div itemprop="text">
          <p>The machine should be installed indoors, in a ventilated area, with:</p><ul><li>Inlet water pressure: 1.5–4 bar</li><li>Temperature: 15 ± 5 °C</li><li>Water quality within set limits (e.g. TDS &lt; 1,000 ppm, hardness &lt; 500 ppm CaCO₃)</li></ul><p>Required connections:</p><ul><li>½" inlet and drain</li><li>230 VAC power supply (max. 0.6 kW)</li><li>Access to a sewer line</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Before operation, ensure proper installation, set up the controller, and verify input conditions. Professional setup is strongly recommended to avoid issues.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</span></div></li>
    
  </ul>

</div>

    </div>
  
          </div>

  
</div>

    </div>
  
